WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.741
How does a tRNA know where to

00:00:01.787 --> 00:00:02.205
go?

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.237
It reads three letters at a time.

00:00:04.573 --> 00:00:06.953
Three mRNA bases make a codon.

00:00:07.488 --> 00:00:09.624
The tRNA has three matching bases, called

00:00:09.647 --> 00:00:10.669
the anticodon.

00:00:11.296 --> 00:00:13.594
Here's the start codon, A-U-G.

00:00:13.931 --> 00:00:16.381
The tRNA with U-A-C pairs with it.

00:00:16.915 --> 00:00:17.902
A matches U.

00:00:18.053 --> 00:00:19.272
U matches A.

00:00:19.411 --> 00:00:20.630
G matches C.

00:00:20.851 --> 00:00:22.511
Like puzzle pieces that only fit their

00:00:22.557 --> 00:00:22.929
match.

00:00:23.219 --> 00:00:25.797
An anticodon is three tRNA bases that

00:00:25.843 --> 00:00:27.898
pair with a matching mRNA codon.

00:00:28.084 --> 00:00:28.711
Swipe.
